be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz calls for unity at CSU party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66619d770c73b27e4c5a057d6655368305a780241fd1f747b0580723c03db210</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-unity-at-csu-party-conference/live-79749353--718b2e6284ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-unity-at-csu-party-conference/live-79749353?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With his coalition under pressure, Merz delivered an address at the close of the CSU conference in Munich. Meanwhile, fire has largely destroyed Hitler's former Eagle's Nest retreat. DW has more</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean leader Kim Jong Un travels to Chinese border city via newly opened bridge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b09639fa6b557d7a5b9b41d3044c66db67fccf911f0d94d13533b37a9ac7415</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T07:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-leader-kim-jong-un-travels-to-chinese-border-city-via-newly-opened-bridge/a-79748580--1461c3f06f45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-leader-kim-jong-un-travels-to-chinese-border-city-via-newly-opened-bridge/a-79748580?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korean leader Kim Jong Un travelled to China’s border city of Dandong via a newly opened bridge linking the two countries, where he met a senior Chinese official.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France protests: More violence feared amid renewed demonstrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:490190885b2485618a0dec41908dc7b504af1fde4dd371744d386209114b8ef0</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T06:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223--43db314a2270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France is deploying some 70,000 police officers as fresh nationwide protests begin. A deadly shooting near Paris has additionally fueled tensions. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japan-Russia ties erode as journalist sits in Moscow jail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21d35a5914fe55fa5d9daf4a7993827038c96cfd5bd3316b2dc982a1f2c25b2f</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-russia-ties-erode-as-journalist-sits-in-moscow-jail/a-79742995--090b57f76cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-russia-ties-erode-as-journalist-sits-in-moscow-jail/a-79742995?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan is demanding access to a journalist who was arrested by Russian security services. The Kremlin claims that Japan is using journalists as spies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Typhoon Champi leaves 1 dead, over 500 injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4779dc9e34407fc3f6982d75c06c2a360aff1cb4e89348161b6bfd428a4380e3</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221--2c62bf3b9cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After killing one person and causing major disruptions in Taiwan, Typhoon Champi is now headed towards China.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Neha Bora refuses to sign peace bond, cites right to democratic dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:666610d05ba9b2a63da288c95ee10add734b3e42d4548460778307b8c2554bcf</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:48:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T04:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-neha-bora-refuses-to-sign-peace-bond-cites-right-to-democratic-dissent/live-79748098--5ec5f3385b66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-neha-bora-refuses-to-sign-peace-bond-cites-right-to-democratic-dissent/live-79748098?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Neha Bora says the peace bond violates the right to democratic dissent. The statement comes amid a wider protest calling for the removal of India's election chief. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hitler's Eagle's Nest retreat catches fire, police say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56b74595395ba459f912bed6155450f542a97deef7163c4823289447dff308e5</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T02:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat-catches-fire-police-say/a-79747820--4006d6d04b27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat-catches-fire-police-say/a-79747820?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities have arrested a suspect as firemen try to put out the fire in Bavaria, near the Austrian border.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France to deploy 70,000 police officers ahead of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:306586e5b5552e65742fadcd87235104a23726b4b6f3096ecbea840c17cfa318</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T22:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-to-deploy-70-000-police-officers-ahead-of-protests/a-79747655--5faa4d329162.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-to-deploy-70-000-police-officers-ahead-of-protests/a-79747655?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With new protests in France planned for this weekend, the authorities pledged to do everything in their power to prevent looting, violence and vandalism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Kenya announces second death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4519dc7f515e2ed3158ab5d22b975001f50f0b0558942138c1843a70fd6104c2</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T21:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-kenya-announces-second-death/a-79747550--9f3288954577.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-kenya-announces-second-death/a-79747550?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kenyan health officials said the 65-year-old ​woman was a close ‌relative of a ‌​man who died of Ebola last month. The woman developed symptoms ‌while under quarantine in Nairobi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump eases Canada tariffs ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e21f8b1280be1b8d4d18eed5c58e2da5243253c922f78f69aec01b7a47468a5c</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T20:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-eases-canada-tariffs-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79747634--d0246e435342.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-eases-canada-tariffs-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79747634?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The move comes as Trump's Republican Party scrambles to maintain control of the US Congress, with a Republican candidate in a key Senate race saying she had lobbied to lift the tariffs on Canadian products.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's attacks on Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, are intensifying. DW asked people on the ground what life is like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6069ff23f283c767f688fa3774236f13a03d5aa0a9d11160eb4caafca269b8c</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-/a-79741090--9d6ca1b7b337.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-is-like/a-79741090?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's attacks on the Ukrainian capital are hitting harder and more frequently, making 2026 one of the long war's bloodiest years for Kyiv. DW asked people on the ground what life is like.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan: Karak church shooting leaves 7 dead, dozens injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28d83f4b35487cca3cdd916597beb082b5f33bb0f6fdeb355a9568fee40b2b64</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jordan-karak-church-shooting-leaves-7-dead-dozens-injured/a-79743535--fb132a258471.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jordan-karak-church-shooting-leaves-7-dead-dozens-injured/a-79743535?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A shooting at a Greek Orthodox church in southern Jordan happened during a funeral, according to authorities. Two unidentified men opened fire on the procession, with Jordan's king vowing "the harshest retaliation."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia, Ukraine agree to US-brokered, 1 city ceasefire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e68967da1a8b70603330df4f8decde4f75a5cec0f83d7943a0956ceb2a9f00bd</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-agree-to-us-brokered-1-city-ceasefire/a-79746723--d5b21a176374.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-agree-to-us-brokered-1-city-ceasefire/a-79746723?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ukrainian city of Oleshky, occupied by Russia and on the frontline, faces a humanitarian crisis. The localized truce comes as Ukrainian President Zelenskyy said negotiators would meet for wider talks next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Afghan women could lose one of their last paths to a higher education</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:578b379d0c2b5cd57abfc19d92fa2988727a506abd59684ada98f5495db7db38</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173--2a76364e2679.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has defunded one of the last universities giving Afghan women the chance to receive an education after the Taliban takeover in 2021. DW spoke with a student who says she's lost hope of ever earning a degree.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Romania blames Russia for ship attack in the Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fb9d7e5bcdd72111d5e8f775a6f8700b501635a2fbf8161dc5d5f079023993d</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romania-blames-russia-for-ship-attack-in-the-black-sea/a-79743425--1bf4cd10b7ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romania-blames-russia-for-ship-attack-in-the-black-sea/a-79743425?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes against ships attempting to export Ukrainian grain and cargo through the western Black Sea have sharply increased this month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine tries to shut Moscow's airports with drone strikes on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08561186b336123810a2234c3d6dcf35bc12815aad6f3ae06787975fbfbf5225</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469--16f9cb7db516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Repeated Ukrainian drone attacks are increasingly disrupting operations at Moscow's airports. The pounding is part of Ukraine's plan to shut down Russia's airpace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Many feared trapped under collapsed building in Nairobi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74eda5273ee52652da55ccb528d9634eec7a7663825d377fc43319233a7bc34f</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/many-feared-trapped-under-collapsed-building-in-nairobi/a-79744598--3192a74714c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/many-feared-trapped-under-collapsed-building-in-nairobi/a-79744598?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">People are feared to be trapped after a large, unfinished building in Nairobi collapsed during construction. Rescue operations have proven complicated as police fired tear gas to disperse looters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda says it has no active Ebola cases, but infections in Kenya and Nigeria are prompting fresh scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85b05148fe9d66fcec28e83974135e2866e5a53849f839c31ffd863a6644152a</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scr/a-79741580--819bf739b307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scrutiny/a-79741580?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Health officials are investigating whether Ebola patients in Kenya and Nigeria crossed paths at Uganda's main airport as conflicting accounts cloud the source of one infection.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Hope, tension and apprehension as voters prepare to elect new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:600634f5f9dbbbc215efcd7cb7b13f92958df24b23d8c0ba221ad5d19a32b15b</id><updated>2026-10-24T12:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102--35e507b36c9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of protests, Serbia faces a pivotal election on Sunday, with a student-led challenge to Aleksandar Vucic's lengthy rule. Allegations of electoral irregularities and fears of a post-election crisis abound.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
